#question(title: [Partitions of different intervals])[
  #set text(size: 13pt)

  Let $a < b < c$. Which of these statements
  are true?

  If any are false, fix them.
  #v(0.1cm)

  + IF $P$ and $Q$ are partitions of
    $[a, b]$,
     #v(0.1cm)

     THEN $P union Q$ is a partition of
     $[a, b]$.
     #v(0.1cm)
  + IF $P$ and $Q$ are partitions of
    $[a, b]$,
     #v(0.1cm)

     THEN $P inter Q$ is a partition of
     $[a, b]$.
     #v(0.1cm)
  + IF $P$ is a partition of $[a, b]$ and $Q$
    is a partition of $[b, c]$
     #v(0.1cm)

     THEN $P union Q$ is a partition of
     $[a, c]$
     #v(0.1cm)
  + IF $P$ is a partition of $[a, c]$,
     #v(0.1cm)

     THEN $P inter [a, b]$ is a partition of
     $[a, b]$
]
